#import "template.typ": policy-rule, policy-warning

= Business Entertaining & Client Hospitality

== Substantive Business Purpose

Entertaining current or prospective clients, key suppliers, or strategic partners is permissible when a clear, direct business benefit to Apex Global Technologies Inc. is demonstrated.

#policy-rule("POL-ENT-001", "Attendee Documentation Mandate")[
  Every entertainment or group dining expense must include:
  + Concrete business objective discussed before, during, or after the event
  + Full roster of attendees, including complete names, company affiliations, and business titles
  + Ratio of company employees to external guests not exceeding 1:1, unless justified in advance
]

== Spending Limits for Client Meals

Hospitality must remain modest, professional, and within defined fiscal limits.

#policy-rule("POL-ENT-002", "Per-Person Entertaining Caps")[
  Reimbursement for hosted meals is capped at:
  - *Client Lunch*: €50.00 / \$55.00 per attendee (including tax and tip)
  - *Client Dinner*: €90.00 / \$100.00 per attendee (including tax and tip)
  Any amount exceeding these caps must be absorbed personally or deducted from the claim before submission.
]

== Alcohol Policy during Client Entertaining

Unlike solo travel, moderate alcohol consumption is recognized in standard business entertainment contexts.

#policy-rule("POL-ENT-003", "Hospitality Alcohol Limitations")[
  Moderate consumption of beer and wine during client dinners is permissible, provided total alcohol expenditure does not exceed thirty percent (30%) of the total food and beverage bill before taxes and tips. Hard spirits, bottle service at nightclubs, and post-dinner bar hopping are strictly prohibited.
]
